{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142138-wolf-blooded-to-uratha-second-change-or-rite-of-passage","id":142138,"title":"Wolf-Blooded to Uratha - Second Change or Rite of Passage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T00:20:42-07:00","id":142138,"title":"Wolf-Blooded to Uratha - Second Change or Rite of Passage?","content":"I run Mortal to Wolf-Blooded to Uratha game now. All players characters are now going through First Change from Mortals to Wolf-Blooded, as we use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/122016-quasi-idigam-chronicles-wolf-blooded\"><b>Idigam Chronicle</b> take on WB with minor werewolves blessings</a>, like ability to shapeshift in to one form or Uratha-like regeneration. Each character also is getting they Auspice on Change night. The problem I got is what to do later, to make those PCs in to proper People. Any <b>Forsaken</b> game line info about First Change beside corebook, especially of Wolf-Blooded, would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> For now I have this two ideas how to make new WB in to Uratha. First, is that character goes through &quot;Second Change&quot;, in which they awaken they fully spiritual half. Maybe they are convulsively jump in to Shadow and back, again, and again. Maybe they come through all five forms under the look of Lunes. Or maybe they got to be possessed by spirit by the night. Main idea is that they are going through uncontrolled &quot;full&quot; transformation, very brutal to them, on the whims of Luna/Moon only plan.<br /> <br /> Second is that Wolf-Blooded can make &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; ( not Rite on Initiation to Tribe ) in that they make very deadly test, and if they make it, Moon and Lunes will blessed them with becoming fully Uratha, not &quot;lesser werewolves&quot; they are now. Example idea I have is typical totem hunt - if pack of Wolf-Blooded send to Shadow Realm return with totem of they own, this spirit and Lunes will teach them how to become one of the People.<br /> <br /> What do you think about them? Maybe you have other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T00:34:20-07:00","id":142148,"title":"","content":"Two books you should pick up, if you can get them: <b>Blood of the Wolf </b>and the <b>Forsaken Chronicler's Guide</b>. I also really suggest picking up some of the oWoD material, such as <b>Possessed</b>; couple it with the <b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b>, and there are ideas from oWoD that are just<i> begging </i>to be poached, reworked and used in the nWoD. Of interest to you might be the Kami.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T01:01:42-07:00","id":142151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142138-wolf-blooded-to-uratha-second-change-or-rite-of-passage?p=142148#post142148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two books you should pick up, if you can get them: <b>Blood of the Wolf </b>and the <b>Forsaken Chronicler's Guide</b>. I also really suggest picking up some of the oWoD material, such as <b>Possessed</b>; couple it with the <b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b>, and there are ideas from oWoD that are just<i> begging </i>to be poached, reworked and used in the nWoD. Of interest to you might be the Kami.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will ask you for what info in what book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I looked quickly yesterday on <b>Blood of Wolf</b>, and it seems to not have anything on First Change, only general stuff about Wolf-Blooded, for example. <b>Forsaken Chronicler's Guide </b>is so hacked in to pieces I would like you to point me in to one of it's parts at least. Other books also would be good for some at least chapters markings, where to look in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T21:50:03-07:00","id":144140,"title":"","content":"I read <b>Blood of Wolf</b> closely and found something interesting in Wolf-Blooded chapter...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood of Wolf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While various rites exist to determine whether a given person will undergo the Change, there\u2019s no way to know. Since the Change can strike at any time during a person\u2019s life, Uratha cannot breathe a sigh of relief (or regret) when a son, daughter or sibling escapes puberty unscathed or completes any other rite of passage without becoming a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Uratha are making various Rites of Passage for Wolf-Blooded to see if they can become proper werewolves. As I see it, hunting for pack totem in Shadow Realm is more and more looking as good way to test limits of WB and change them in to Uratha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:31:35-07:00","id":144191,"title":"","content":"Well the rites of passage depend on the tribe. Tribes of the moon and Lore of the forsaken will set that for you. I might recommend making all the players of the same tribe initially so you don't have to do all the different sessions on semantics. <br /> <br /> Pick up the storytellers handbook revised as well. No matter what series its some damn good stuff. You can find it in werewolf the apocalypse section on drive through rpg. Hell...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/61536/Werewolf-Storytellers-Handbook-Revised?cPath=1_6536\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/61536.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/61536/Werewolf-Storytellers-Handbook-Revised?cPath=1_6536\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf Storytellers Handbook Revised - White Wolf | Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/61536/Werewolf-Storytellers-Handbook-Revised?cPath=1_6536\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/61536/Werewolf-Storytellers-Handbook-Revised?cPath=1_6536 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Werewolf Storytellers Handbook Revised - Song of the End Times From the secrets of the highest-ranking elders to the cryptic lore of the Triat; from the blasphem </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Has some good stuff in it. Like how not to bone up a story. Info I know I needed. I've gone from trying to make epic chronicles to simple 4-5 scene segments. They're a lot better for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:48:10-07:00","id":144465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142138-wolf-blooded-to-uratha-second-change-or-rite-of-passage?p=144191#post144191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the rites of passage depend on the tribe. Tribes of the moon and Lore of the forsaken will set that for you. I might recommend making all the players of the same tribe initially so you don't have to do all the different sessions on semantics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was more thinking about Totem hunting, as <b>it is</b> a Rite of Passage ( of sort ) for new pack, isn't it? I like variety of characters in my games, and was really hoping for multiple Firstborns to play as Narrator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> After they would become proper pack - and by this, proper Uratha - I would like to make one on one game sessions with players of they Rite of Initiation to their Tribe (under the Firstborn direct look, but it's different matter).<br /> <br /> So for &quot;changing test&quot; I look for something rather universal and moderate easy for Uratha - so all Wolf-Blooded could logically partake, and bar will be left high on them. They should <b>really</b> earn status of &quot;true&quot; werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142138-wolf-blooded-to-uratha-second-change-or-rite-of-passage?p=144191#post144191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has some good stuff in it. Like how not to bone up a story. Info I know I needed. I've gone from trying to make epic chronicles to simple 4-5 scene segments. They're a lot better for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely will look on this. Too be true, <b>Werewolf: Apocalypse</b> was my second WoD game ever read, and to this day I'm sad I didn't get to run Fenris <i>Rite of Passage</i> adventure I was having. But I hell lot a more like the <b>Forsaken</b> as gameline and will happily part some story advice from it's predecessor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:09:57-07:00","id":144582,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse has good stuff in it for narration and ideas, it just tends to be lacking in certain areas that I feel forsaken does better. Really though it's apples and oranges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}